solution:
Wrap each rendered table in its own region with max-width: 100%, overflow-x: auto, and horizontal overscroll containment. Keep border-collapse on the table. Give the region a visible keyboard focus style and an accessible name so keyboard users can reach offscreen columns.

Add a mobile viewport meta tag and use explicit cell borders with sufficient contrast in both themes. Apply the wrapper in the shared table renderer so all Markdown tables follow the same rule.

```css
.table-scroll {
  max-width: 100%;
  overflow-x: auto;
  overscroll-behavior-x: contain;
}
```
